  "script": "The M5 CS was designed to be lighter and quicker, shedding 256 pounds compared to the standard M5. BMW produced 1,132 M5 CS sedans worldwide, with 454 allocated to the United States, and over half of all units were finished in Frozen Deep Green. At its heart, a 4.4L twin-turbo V8 engine. Inside, M carbon bucket seats and a 16-speaker Harman/Kardon stereo create a performance-focused yet luxurious atmosphere. The M5 CS boasts 627 hp and 553 lb-ft of torque. Its drivetrain allows dynamic switching between all-wheel and rear-wheel drive, offering both grip and excitement on demand. Though it started at around $142,000 new, the M5 CS holds its value remarkably well, trading for about $172,233 today, reflecting a strong investment. With jaw-dropping speed, upscale features, and a limited run, does the exclusivity and performance make the M5 CS the ultimate sedan?",
